From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:26:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] virtio-media: raise the shadow buffer to 256 KiB for 4K

A 4K RGBA decoder output could not be queued: QBUF's SG entry array
did not fit the 64 KiB shadow buffer (RPi5 DomA, HEVC 3840x2160, a
33,177,600-byte AB24 plane):

    virtio-media: 5911 SG entries (94576 bytes) do not fit the
                  remaining 65536 bytes of the shadow buffer
    V4L2Device: (CAPTURE_MPLANE)VIDIOC_QBUF failed

A fully fragmented 4K plane needs 8100 entries, 129,600 bytes. Make
the buffer 256 KiB, the size of qemu's command buffer
(VIRTIO_MEDIA_CMD_BUF_SIZE), and update the two comments that said 4K
does not fit. The buffer stays kmalloc'd: it has to be physically
contiguous for one descriptor, so the allocation becomes order-6, once
per open session, on every board that runs this driver.

Change-Id: I90efc5bab420784faccf3e29502b3b4048dad48a
Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/driver/session.h
+++ b/driver/session.h
@@ -18,30 +18,31 @@
 #define VIRTIO_MEDIA_LAST_QUEUE (V4L2_BUF_TYPE_META_OUTPUT)
 
 /*
- * Size of the per-session virtio shadow and event buffers.
+ * Size of the per-session virtio shadow buffer.
  *
- * 64 KiB, because a 1080p RGBA frame does not fit in 16 KiB. The output is
- * RGBA when the guest's GL has no GL_EXT_YUV_target (an NV12 EGLImage then
- * cannot be used as a texture), and RGBA at 1920x1088 is 8,355,840 B =
- * 2040 pages. Measured on RPi4, 2026-09-04:
+ * 256 KiB, because a 4K RGBA frame's SG entry array has to fit. The output
+ * is RGBA when the guest's GL has no GL_EXT_YUV_target (an NV12 EGLImage
+ * then cannot be used as a texture). Each page of a plane is one 16-byte
+ * virtio_media_sg_entry unless the exporter coalesces contiguous pages:
  *
- *     virtio-media: 2033 SG entries (32528 bytes) do not fit the
- *                   remaining 16384 bytes of the shadow buffer
+ *   1920x1088 RGBA   8,355,840 B   2040 pages    32,640 B of entries
+ *   3840x2160 RGBA  33,177,600 B   8100 pages   129,600 B of entries
  *
- * At 64 KiB those entries (16 B x 2033 = 32,528 B) fit alongside the
- * staging of the command structure and its payload. 4K RGBA
- * (3840x2160x4 = 33,177,600 B = 8100 pages = 129,600 B of entries) does not
- * fit; that needs the entry array split across several descriptors, which
- * is not implemented.
+ * Measured: 1080p needed 2033 entries (RPi4, 2026-09-04: "do not fit the
+ * remaining 16384 bytes"), 4K 5911 entries = 94,576 B (RPi5, 2026-10-15:
+ * "do not fit the remaining 65536 bytes"). 256 KiB holds a fully
+ * fragmented 4K plane with room for the command and its payload, and is
+ * the size of qemu's command buffer (VIRTIO_MEDIA_CMD_BUF_SIZE), so a
+ * larger one could not be sent anyway.
  *
  * kmalloc returns physically contiguous memory, so the SG entry array placed
  * in the shadow buffer is still describable by one descriptor. That
  * assumption is required -- scatterlist_builder.c takes virt_to_page +
- * offset and looks only at the first page -- and it holds at 64 KiB too.
- * The allocation is order-4, so on failure the session cannot be opened
- * (err_shadow_buf).
+ * offset and looks only at the first page -- which rules out kvmalloc. The
+ * allocation is order-6, made once per open session, so on failure the
+ * session cannot be opened (err_shadow_buf).
  */
-#define VIRTIO_SHADOW_BUF_SIZE 0x10000
+#define VIRTIO_SHADOW_BUF_SIZE 0x40000
 
 /**
  * struct virtio_media_dmabuf - Cached import of one V4L2_MEMORY_DMABUF plane.
--- a/driver/scatterlist_builder.c
+++ b/driver/scatterlist_builder.c
@@ -702,12 +702,10 @@
 		 * entry array -- at 16 bytes per virtio_media_sg_entry.
 		 *
 		 * A guest GL without GL_EXT_YUV_target makes the decoder
-		 * output RGBA. A 1920x1088 RGBA frame is 8,355,840 bytes =
-		 * 2040 pages, and its sg_table measured 2033 entries =
-		 * 32,528 bytes (RPi4, 2026-09-04), which fits. 4K RGBA
-		 * (33,177,600 bytes = 8100 pages = 129,600 bytes of entries)
-		 * does not fit and needs the entry array split across
-		 * descriptors, which is not done here.
+		 * output RGBA: 129,600 bytes of entries for a fully
+		 * fragmented 4K frame, which the 256 KiB buffer holds (see
+		 * session.h). An array larger than the buffer would have to
+		 * be split across descriptors, which is not done here.
 		 *
 		 * A fully fragmented 1080p NV12 plane is 3110400 bytes = 760
 		 * 4 KiB pages, which fits with margin (and contiguous runs
